    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0994" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower
                    Library, Dulles papers, “Meetings with
                    the President”</note>
                <head>No. 417<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-12-01">December 1,
                            1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum of Luncheon
                        Conversation with the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d417-f1"/></p>
                <p>We discussed the position vis-à-vis Communist China, particularly with reference
                    to the imprisonment of the United States flyers. The President reaffirmed his
                    support of the position which I had taken in my speech the night before,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d417-f2"/> after communicating with him through Hagerty at Augusta.</p>
                <p>The President felt that we should push this matter vigorously in the United
                    Nations and asked me to talk to Ambassador Lodge. I said this accorded very much with my own thinking.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion of unrelated matters.]</p>
                <closer><signed>JFD<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d417-f3"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d417-f1" n="1" xml:id="d417-f1-content">
                <p>Dulles had lunch with the President on
                    Nov. 30; this apparently refers to that conversation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d417-f2" n="2" xml:id="d417-f2-content">
                <p>Nov. 29.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d417-f3" n="3" xml:id="d417-f3-content">
                <p>Initialed for Dulles by O’Connor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
